        fp: "An engineering company contracted in writing with a municipal water district to design and oversee the installation of an industrial water filtration pump station for $500,000[cite: 42]. Under the contract, progress payments of $50,000 were payable monthly upon presentation of an independent supervising architect's certificate of satisfactory completion[cite: 42]. For the sixth progress payment, the engineer timely completed the specified work in full conformity with all engineering standards and contract blueprints[cite: 42]. However, the supervising architect, harboring intense personal animosity toward the engineering company's chief executive officer following a bitter private divorce dispute, arbitrarily and maliciously refused to issue the certificate, stating privately: 'I will never sign off on any project of yours.'[cite: 42] The water district refused to release the $50,000 progress payment solely because the certificate was missing[cite: 42]. The engineering company sued the water district for the $50,000 installment[cite: 42].",
