            "No, because an oral agreement to extend a closing date without fresh consideration is void under the pre-existing duty rule.",
            "Yes, because the landlord's oral statement operated as a waiver of the timing condition, which became irrevocable through the investor's detrimental reliance.",
            "Yes, because 'time is of the essence' clauses in commercial real estate sales are void per se as against public policy."
